1561
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:54,020
The Treasure of Hers and the Prince

1562
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:54,020
The Treasure of Hers and the Prince

1563
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:54,020
The Treasure of Hers and the Prince

1564
00:04:53,980 --> 00:05:00,070
Is this the young lady
the chick tried to frantically take back from the tanuki?

1565
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:01,440
Tanuki?

1566
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,030
Hey.

1567
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:05,110
Want to hear an old story about this young lad?

1568
00:05:05,110 --> 00:05:09,000
If you pay for the drinks, I'll tell you some things
that may or may not be true!

1569
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:16,130
I'm Elianna. It's an honor to meet you, Doctor.

1570
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,050
That aside, I have a request!

1571
00:05:19,050 --> 00:05:19,740
Hm?

1572
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:22,760
I'd like you to take me to the chief of the Stars of Thistle.

1573
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:27,640
Why's some Sauslind knight want to see the chief?
Planning to attack him or something?

1574
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:30,770
I just want to talk.

1575
00:05:30,770 --> 00:05:35,250
Think of this mediating as repayment to someone
you extorted out of money for alcohol.

1576
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:41,050
Eh? You treated me only once, it's not worth it.

1577
00:05:41,050 --> 00:05:44,280
Rene. Go on and head home to your mother.

1578
00:05:44,770 --> 00:05:46,730
We'll be there later.

1579
00:05:51,860 --> 00:05:53,030
Lord Chris.

1580
00:05:54,230 --> 00:05:58,550
How did you come to know one of the Stars of Thistle?

1581
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:01,170
Uh… Er, I'll tell you later.

1582
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:04,740
Let's head out now.

1583
00:06:06,970 --> 00:06:11,180
Well… I'm going to escort Rene.

1584
00:06:17,910 --> 00:06:18,860
Eli?

1585
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:24,610
<i>Though I should be dealing with
the Bernstein family matter,</i>

1586
00:06:24,610 --> 00:06:28,830
<i>somehow I can't be by His Highness' side right now.</i>

1587
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:34,460
<i>Since I got here, I've seen
a different side of the prince than I normally do.</i>

1588
00:06:35,290 --> 00:06:37,460
<i>Though on one hand I am happy,</i>

1589
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:42,970
<i>the fact that there's a past 
that I'm unaware of also leads to anxiety.</i>

1590
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:51,220
<i>But what causes me the most anxiety is that
I can't remember a single thing from when I met His Highness.</i>

1591
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:53,730
Lady Elianna.

1592
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:55,290
Are you all right?

1593
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,150
Lord Alan…

1594
00:06:58,150 --> 00:07:03,620
Please don't keep everything bottled up.
If you feel anxious or upset make sure to tell Lord Chris.

1595
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:09,660
If you don't, Glen will be the target of his anger
and he'll be discouraged.

1596
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:14,310
Okay. I'm sorry. I didn't mean to worry you.

1597
00:07:15,170 --> 00:07:16,750
Let's go, Miss!

1598
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:17,670
Sure.

1599
00:07:18,290 --> 00:07:19,850
Rene! Paolo!

1600
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:22,420
Hey guys!

1601
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:25,880
You two are okay?

1602
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:26,840
Yeah!

1603
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,180
This lady and her friends helped us!

1604
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:34,600
We thought you'd gotten caught.

1605
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:38,190
We told that mole noble
we weren't listening to another word he said.

1606
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,760
After that he got upset

1607
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:43,690
and locked up Rene's mom in that mansion.

1608
00:07:43,690 --> 00:07:44,820
What?!

1609
00:07:43,690 --> 00:07:44,820
Huh?!

1610
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:46,470
She is?!

1611
00:07:46,470 --> 00:07:48,200
I'll be right back.

1612
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:54,080
He said he's gonna burn all the books
to get rid of the evidence too.

1613
00:07:55,410 --> 00:07:58,790
We came back because we want to talk to the chief.

1614
00:07:59,530 --> 00:08:01,420
Burn the books...?

1615
00:08:01,770 --> 00:08:02,670
Huh?

1616
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:06,090
Where is he?! Where is that noble?!

1617
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:12,350
Not only is Rene's mother locked up,
he'd resort to such a barbaric act as burning books!

1618
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:14,850
He can't even be considered human any more!

1619
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:17,850
I'll take you there!

1620
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:20,100
This way!

1621
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,440
Lady Elianna?!

1622
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:23,590
You're the bad guys!

1623
00:08:23,590 --> 00:08:24,980
N-No!

1624
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,750
Wait!

1625
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:38,750
What a diabolical thing to do!

1626
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:42,500
I know you!

1627
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:48,840
<i>He's always around His Highness at social events.
I believe his name is…</i>

1628
00:08:49,290 --> 00:08:50,340
Baron Mole!

1629
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:51,840
It's "Maudsley"!

1630
00:08:52,350 --> 00:08:55,700
Even an animal wouldn't burn books!

1631
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:57,850
This is absolutely inexcusable!

1632
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:01,270
You're worse than a cockroach!
You ought to be ashamed!

1633
00:09:01,270 --> 00:09:03,270
A-A cockroach…

1634
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:13,200
It's obvious that you used children to steal books
and deceived others with my family name!

1635
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:18,160
At least have the backbone to admit to your crimes,
and give Rene's mother back to us.

1636
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:23,500
Lady Elianna, what are you saying
after such a sudden appearance?

1637
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:28,050
Do you actually believe what these wandering savages say?

1638
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:32,420
Well then, what do you have to say
for those books over there?

1639
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:35,190
These are books I myself have purchased.

1640
00:09:35,190 --> 00:09:39,270
He's lying! That man ordered us to go and steal books!

1641
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:41,690
And you said you were a Bernstein!

1642
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:44,520
Preposterous!

1643
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:48,940
Now then, Lady Elianna, shall we make a deal?

1644
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,690
A deal?

1645
00:09:51,040 --> 00:10:00,120
I will keep that you, the fiancée of the Crown Prince,
are mingling with these disgusting rabble.

1646
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:06,090
In return for that, you will discontinue
those ridiculous measures you are currently promoting.

1647
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:07,590
Measures?

1648
00:10:07,590 --> 00:10:10,920
I refuse to believe that they would
pass the budget on to something like that

1649
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:14,550
and let business negotiations
with the Bass Company slip away!

1650
00:10:14,550 --> 00:10:19,900
The Bass Company is currently attempting
to undertake the manufacture of new weapons!

1651
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,770
Our kingdom should seize this opportunity

1652
00:10:22,770 --> 00:10:26,000
before it is passed along to another country,
by any means necessary.

1653
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,980
This is for the sake of our country's future!

1654
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:33,050
I think it would be better for our country's future

1655
00:10:33,050 --> 00:10:38,200
if we were to allot expenses towards
the research of curing illnesses amongst our people

1656
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:40,830
rather than developing weapons to hurt others.

1657
00:10:40,830 --> 00:10:47,250
Our ancestors said it best: "If a place burns books,
they will burn human beings in the end as well."

1658
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:53,880
This is not a route I wish for our country to take.

1659
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:56,890
Therefore, I cannot accept your "deal".

1660
00:10:57,140 --> 00:11:02,460
You can only spin your petty and cunning speeches
because you shield yourself behind the Prince's authority.

1661
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:06,150
It seems I shall have to resolve the matter through force.

1662
00:11:06,150 --> 00:11:07,400
Miss...

1663
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:12,900
Stop right there.

1664
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:19,030
Your Highness...

1665
00:11:19,350 --> 00:11:23,040
P-Prince Christopher... What are you doing here?!

1666
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,640
This is outrageous.

1667
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:31,170
Come now, Baron Maudsley, there's no possible way
I'd let Eli face danger by herself.

1668
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:34,170
Your Highness, I-I haven't done a thing...

1669
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:39,890
I beg you, pay no mind to what
those scamps from the Stars of Thistle have said!

1670
00:11:39,890 --> 00:11:41,930
After all, their people are a filthy lot.

1671
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:44,980
I am a noble devoted to my country,

1672
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:49,690
and as an intelligent royal you should understand
who is more worthy of your trust!

1673
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:58,070
Leaving that aside, the main issue at the moment
is that <i>your</i> troops are pointing their swords at my fiancée.

1674
00:11:58,340 --> 00:11:59,740
Oh, about that...

1675
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:00,950
Moreover...

1676
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:05,480
it seems you have an extreme derision
for the people of the Stars of Thistle,

1677
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:10,390
However, I will listen to what they have to say,
and I will do it without partiality.

1678
00:12:12,210 --> 00:12:15,010
Please wait, Prince Christopher!

1679
00:12:15,010 --> 00:12:18,970
Do you not understand what must be done
for the sake of the country?!

1680
00:12:19,350 --> 00:12:23,060
There's one more thing
I forgot to mention, Baron Maudsley.

1681
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:29,600
The Bass Company, the weapons manufacturer that you glorified,
has somehow been horribly scammed.

1682
00:12:30,390 --> 00:12:31,110
Eh?!

1683
00:12:31,110 --> 00:12:34,710
There was an old man involved in the field who professed

1684
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:38,700
that no one could surpass him
when it comes to weapon development.

1685
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:43,870
When the weapons were finished, made according
to the blueprints he had written, they were all defective.

1686
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:45,870
Th-There's no way!

1687
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:51,220
Now then, why is the Bass Company
now in the throes of bankruptcy?

1688
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:55,630
On top of that, I heard that he was swindled
out of a large amount of money for alcohol and ran away.

1689
00:12:55,630 --> 00:12:56,630
Huh?!

1690
00:12:56,870 --> 00:12:59,760
Some elderly men out there can certainly be troublesome.

1691
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:04,760
H-How absurd...

1692
00:13:07,070 --> 00:13:07,930
Arrest him!

1693
00:13:10,770 --> 00:13:13,150
What? Has everything been wrapped up?

1694
00:13:13,150 --> 00:13:14,650
I didn't get any stage time?

1695
00:13:14,650 --> 00:13:15,520
You're late.

1696
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:18,030
Aw, I was hurrying as quickly I could, too...

1697
00:13:19,410 --> 00:13:20,300
Eli.

1698
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:26,700
I-I'm so terribly sorry!
I chose to take action all on my own and—

1699
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,290
Good grief.

1700
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:36,300
I can't take my eyes off of you for a second.

1701
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:38,300
Y-Your Highn—

1702
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:45,300
There aren't many princesses who will march
into a scoundrel's lair without waiting for the prince.

1703
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:48,390
P-Please forgive me.

1704
00:13:48,390 --> 00:13:51,310
Um, are you angry with me?

1705
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,230
Does it look like I am?

1706
00:13:53,230 --> 00:13:55,310
Mister! Miss!

1707
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:58,570
They said my mom's inside! I'm going in there!

1708
00:13:58,990 --> 00:14:00,780
Shall we go too?

1709
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:02,070
Yes.

1710
00:14:03,860 --> 00:14:04,570
Mom!

1711
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:08,230
Rene...

1712
00:14:08,810 --> 00:14:10,730
Is it okay for you to get up?

1713
00:14:10,730 --> 00:14:13,620
Yes. And Paolo is here too.

1714
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:17,730
Eli?

1715
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:23,150
It's, well... she reminds me of my mother.

1716
00:14:24,310 --> 00:14:29,220
Mom, I met a knight of Sauslind
who has the same blue eyes as me.

1717
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:32,580
I thought he was my dad.

1718
00:14:34,420 --> 00:14:37,730
He told me a fairy tale.

1719
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:41,670
It was about a blue-eyed boy and a princess,

1720
00:14:41,670 --> 00:14:48,240
and the princess told him magic words
to break the evil spell his mother was under.

1721
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:52,250
He said that important things can't be seen with the eye.

1722
00:14:53,590 --> 00:14:54,950
That was...

1723
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:57,960
And the knight told me something.

1724
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:02,710
You must not lose sight of what is important to you.

1725
00:15:03,430 --> 00:15:06,560
You know, I already knew it.

1726
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:10,970
My dad isn't alive anymore.

1727
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:12,980
Rene...

1728
00:15:14,850 --> 00:15:18,650
Mom, I'm not gonna run away
from the truth anymore.

1729
00:15:18,650 --> 00:15:24,360
I'm one of the Stars of Thistle, after all,
and we always continue to seek for the truth.

1730
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:36,250
Rene.

1731
00:15:37,910 --> 00:15:43,980
Sauslind has started building a charity hospital
that brings together doctors and herbalists,

1732
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:48,690
and an institution specializing in disease
just about ten days ago.

1733
00:15:48,690 --> 00:15:50,180
It has?

1734
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:53,390
It will be a hospital that anyone can come to freely.

1735
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:56,020
Even us, in the Stars of Thistle?!

1736
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:57,520
Of course.

1737
00:15:57,750 --> 00:15:58,730
Wow!

1738
00:15:58,730 --> 00:15:59,940
Awesome!

1739
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:01,270
Miss, this is great!

1740
00:16:01,630 --> 00:16:02,940
Yes!

1741
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:10,410
The country is running it,
but the name of the person in charge is, Elianna Bernstein.

1742
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:11,910
Huh?

1743
00:16:11,910 --> 00:16:16,410
Your Highness... why am I in charge?

1744
00:16:16,410 --> 00:16:18,420
Because you originally proposed the idea.

1745
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:20,420
I-I did?

1746
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,670
That's right.

1747
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:26,670
Elianna, why do you like books so much?

1748
00:16:27,050 --> 00:16:29,650
Because I'm looking for my mom.

1749
00:16:29,650 --> 00:16:30,970
Your mom?

1750
00:16:30,970 --> 00:16:38,370
Yes. My mom died three years ago,
so I hardly have any memories of her.

1751
00:16:38,370 --> 00:16:44,320
That's why I read the books my mom loved
and think about what she liked about them.

1752
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:50,190
When I do that, I feel I'm talking with my mom.

1753
00:16:50,950 --> 00:16:58,960
Also, I just need to find out if there was a way
to cure my mom back then.

1754
00:17:00,010 --> 00:17:08,970
I wish there were a library made of doctors
just like there are libraries made of books.

1755
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:11,040
A library of doctors...

1756
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:19,880
If there's a library of doctors, there may be fewer people like me,
fewer that wept and mourned the loss of their mothers.

1757
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:24,370
It'd be nice to have a charity hospital
where anyone can be seen.

1758
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:29,610
Your Highness, you remember such an old conversation?

1759
00:17:33,850 --> 00:17:36,120
Even still, I...

1760
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:37,950
What's going on, Miss?

1761
00:17:37,950 --> 00:17:43,130
You said that you're not sure if you are lovers,
but it looks like you're super into him.

1762
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:47,670
Oh? Did you really say that, Eli?

1763
00:17:47,670 --> 00:17:49,380
Um... you see...

1764
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:51,880
Eli, please tell me why...

1765
00:17:53,610 --> 00:17:58,930
Please don't keep everything bottled up.
If you feel anxious or upset make sure to tell Lord Chris.

1766
00:18:00,050 --> 00:18:06,500
I... It's been on my mind since the other day,
but... I don't remember.

1767
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:09,440
I don't remember when we met a long time ago.

1768
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,030
Eli...

1769
00:18:11,330 --> 00:18:13,030
I'm so very sorry.

1770
00:18:13,030 --> 00:18:18,540
Your Highness has cherished
all of these memories of me like this, and yet...

1771
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:21,040
Eli! Elianna!

1772
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,670
Y-Your Highness, we are in company!

1773
00:18:25,110 --> 00:18:31,380
Eli, I'm so happy! I never dreamed you were
working so hard to try and remember our past.

1774
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:32,360
Um...

1775
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:33,970
C'mon, Miss.

1776
00:18:34,250 --> 00:18:36,850
You can just kiss him, right?

1777
00:18:36,850 --> 00:18:37,960
Pardon?

1778
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:43,350
I mean, you know that old saying. The spell cast on the princess
can be broken by the prince's kiss.

1779
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:46,650
Well, you heard him. Why don't we give it a try?

1780
00:18:46,650 --> 00:18:48,110
No, that's quite all right!

1781
00:18:48,590 --> 00:18:49,860
How about the magic words, then?

1782
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:50,940
Huh?

1783
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:54,240
The spell on the princess
can be broken by magic words, right?

1784
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:58,240
Magic words... magic words...

1785
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:01,050
What's important is always invisible.

1786
00:19:01,050 --> 00:19:04,750
The magic words you told me broke the spell.

1787
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:11,880
Elianna. The next time we meet,
I'll tell you some magic words that only you'll know.

1788
00:19:16,230 --> 00:19:17,510
What is it?

1789
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,450
I remember it!

1790
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:29,280
Thank you!

1791
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,110
See ya!

1792
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:40,120
Young man, remember,
the Stars of Thistle are always watching.

1793
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:47,120
The Star Traveler was probably written
by someone in the Stars of Thistle.

1794
00:19:47,730 --> 00:19:48,630
Hm?

1795
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:55,420
Eli, how did you remember that thing from so long ago?

1796
00:19:57,590 --> 00:20:02,260
Well... um, in the end,
part of it was that I wanted to remember.

1797
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:07,390
After all, it <i>was</i> something from a long time ago
that allowed me to be by your side right now.

1798
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:13,940
I felt that since I could not remember
it wasn't right for me to be with you.

1799
00:20:13,940 --> 00:20:17,780
So I thought I should remember.

1800
00:20:18,850 --> 00:20:19,660
Thank you.

1801
00:20:21,370 --> 00:20:28,580
Okay, I'll be honest with you.
The truth is, at first, I was worried.

1802
00:20:29,590 --> 00:20:30,580
Huh?

1803
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:33,090
People change.

1804
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:42,600
And the situation with your mother...
I thought you may have changed in the time I didn't see you.

1805
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,080
Your Highness...

1806
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:50,600
But nothing about you changed.
You remained the bibliophile princess that I knew.

1807
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:55,730
But even though I see much of you
unchanged in these past four years,

1808
00:20:55,730 --> 00:21:00,130
I've also seen that you have grown to be
a little different then you were long ago,

1809
00:21:00,130 --> 00:21:03,240
and I fell in love with you all over again, Elianna.

1810
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:06,870
It's the same for me.

1811
00:21:06,870 --> 00:21:13,750
In these four years, I've come to think of Your Highness
as more precious to me than books.

1812
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:15,530
Eli...

1813
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:22,760
Important things can't be seen with the eye.

1814
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:26,890
The magic words you told me broke the spell.

1815
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:28,520
Thank you.

1816
00:21:28,520 --> 00:21:30,500
You're welcome.

1817
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:36,500
Elianna. The next time we meet,
I'll tell you some secret magic words that only you will know.

1818
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:45,270
Your Highness, will you tell me those secret magic words
you promised you would that day?

1819
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,500
Eli.

1820
00:21:57,840 --> 00:22:00,220
You are my treasure.

